#
# WP-SCP-022 020K R1 + R2 safety reviews (2026-04-30): expanded path
# coverage to close 7 MAJ + 4 MIN findings — the canonical §4 020K
# spec was minimal; the broader rules below close audit-trail tamper,
# signing-key substitution, onboarding-contract weakening, retroactive
# spec tampering, findings manipulation, workflow-selftest harness
# bypass, supply-chain monitoring drift, and CODEOWNERS-itself tamper.
# Coverage broadenings vs the canonical spec:
#   tests/conflict_gate/** → tests/**       (R2-SAFE-013 selftest harness)
#   .github/workflows/**   → .github/**     (R2-SAFE-014 dependabot.yml)
#   + docs/integrations/**                  (R2-SAFE-017 doctrine docs)
#   + /CODEOWNERS self-protection           (R2-SAFE-015 ordering self-tamper)
#
# ORDERING INVARIANT (SAFE-009): GitHub CODEOWNERS is last-match-
# wins. Any future broad-wildcard rule (e.g. `docs/** @<reviewer>`
# or `output/** @<reviewer>`) MUST be added BEFORE this block, or
# the broad rule will silently override the specific governance
# rules. New specific governance rules go at the END of this block
# to preserve coverage. The `/CODEOWNERS` self-protection rule is
# the final line by design — it must remain last so any reordering
# attempt routes through @jrnb2024 review. Re-verify ordering
# whenever this file is touched.
